{"id":"word:hebrew:H3956","type":"word","title":"לָשׁוֹן","subtitle":"H3956 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"the tongue (of man or animals), used literally (as the instrument of licking, eating, or speech), and figuratively (speech, an ingot, a fork of flame, a cove of water)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to לָשׁוֹן (H3956) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 117 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"לָשׁוֹן (lâshôwn) means the tongue (of man or animals), used literally (as the instrument of licking, eating, or speech), and figuratively (speech, an ingot, a fork of flame, a cove of water) First listed occurrence: 2Sam 23 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"לָשׁוֹן","transliteration":"lâshôwn","pronunciation":"law-shone'","strong":"H3956","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3956","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["לְשׁ֣וֹן","לָשׁ֖וֹן","לְשׁוֹנָ֑/ם","לְשֹׁנֽ/וֹ","לָשֽׁוֹן"],"morphs":[["HNcbsc",20],["HNcbsa",17],["HNcbsc/Sp3mp",12],["HNcbsc/Sp3ms",8],["HNcbsc/Sp1cs",7],["HR/Ncbsc/Sp3ms",6],["HC/Ncbsc",5],["HR/Ncbsc",4],["HC/Ncbsc/Sp3ms",4],["HR/Ncbsc/Sp1cs",4]]},"definitions":{"short":"the tongue (of man or animals), used literally (as the instrument of licking, eating, or speech), and figuratively (speech, an ingot, a fork of flame, a cove of water)","usage":"babbler, bay, evil speaker, language, talker, tongue, wedge.","full":"H3956. lashon לָשׁוֺן noun masculine Josh 7:21 and (more often) feminine Isa 28:11 tongue (Late Hebrew id. ; also Assyrian lišânu ; Arabic ; Ethiopic ; Aramaic לִישָּׁן לִשָּׁן, , (all li- ); Zinjirli לשן DHM Sendsch. 59 ); — absolute ׳ל Exod 4:10 +; הַלָּשֹׁן Josh 15:2 ; construct לְשׁוֺן 7:21 +; suffix לְשׁוֺנִי 2Sam 23:2 ; לְשֹׁנוֺ Exod 11:7 2 t.; לְשׁוֺנוֺ Judg 7:5 ; Est 1:22 ; לְשׁוֺנְךָ Psa 34:14 ; לְשׁוֺנְכֶם Isa 59:3 , etc.; plural לְשֹׁנוֺת absolute Psa 31:21 ; Isa 66:18 ; construct Zech 8:23 ; suffix לְשֹׁנֹתָם Gen 10:20 , 31 ; &#8212; 1 tongue of men, a. used in lapping Judg 7:5 ; cleaving to the palate ( חֵק ), in thirst Lam 4:4 , so as to produce dumbness Job 29:10 (|| נֶחְבָּא קוֺל ), Psa 137:6 ; Ezek 3:26 (|| נֶאֱלַם ); cleaving to jaws ( מַלְקוֺחַ ) Psa 22:16 ; ׳ל נָשָׁ֑תָּה בַּצָּמָא Isa 41:17 their tongue for thirst is parched ; ׳לְ בְּפִיהֶם תִּמַּק Zech 14:12 (of ׳י s judgment); a choice morsel is held ל ׳תַּחַת Job 20:12 (figurative of mischief), compare Psa 10:7 (ready to be uttered), 66:17 (|| מֶּה ), Song 4:11 . b. usually as organ of speech, both good and bad (especially Psalms, Proverbs, often || שָׂפָה מֶּה, ); — ל ׳כְּבַד Exod 4:10 (J) heavy of tongue ; ל ׳מַעֲנֵה Prov 16:1 , עַללְֿשׁוֺנִי מִלָּתוֺ 2Sam 23:2 , compare Prov 31:26 ; Psa 139:4 ( ׳בִּל ), עַוְלָה בִּלְשׁוֺנִי הֲיֵשׁ Job 6:30 ; ל בְּיַד וְחַיִּים ׳מָוֶת Prov 18:21 , compare 21:23 ; 25:15 ; of (false) prophets, ל ׳הַלֹּקְהִים Jer 23:31 ; subject of verb of speaking, בֶּר Di — לְשׁוֺנִי דִּבְּרָה בִחִכִּי Job 33:2 ; Psa 12:4 ; 37:30 ; compare ( Jer 9:7 below and) לְדַבֵּר ׳ל תְּמַהֵר ֗֗֗ Isa 32:4 , מָהִיר סֹפֵר עֵט לְשׁוֺנִי Psa 45:2 , i.e. as swift as a rapid scribe's stylus; subject of הָגָה Isa 59:3 ; Job 27:4 ; Psa 35:28 ; 71:24 ; subject of נִשְׁבַּע Isa 45:23 ; ׳ל בָּאָרֶץ תִּהַלַךְ Psa 73:9 ; of hostile speech, insolence, etc., Josh 10:21 (J E; object of I. חָרַץ q. v., compare 3 below), Jer 18:18 ; Isa 3:8 ; ל ׳זַעַם Hosea 7:16 (but text dubious, compare We Now), ׳ל חַדָּה חֶרֶב Psa 57:6 , compare 64:4 ; ל שָֽׁנְנוּ ׳נָחָשׁ כְּמוֺ 140:4 ; ׳כָּללֿ אִתָּךְ תָּקוּם Isa 54:17 ; ל ׳הֶאֱרִיךְ 57:4 ; further, Jer 9:2 ; 9:4 ; as instrument of seductive flattery ( הֶחֱלִיק ), without בְּ , Psa 5:10 ; Proverbs 28:33, compare לָ חֶלְקַת ׳נָכְרִיָּה Prov 6:24 ;. of falsehood Psa 78:36 (compare below); of slander (compare לושֵׁן ) עַללֿ ׳רָגַל 15:3 , לָשׁוֺן אִישׁ 140:12 , compare ׳לְ סָ֑תֶר Proverbs 25:33; בְּל ׳חָטָא 39:2 ; compare 64:9 (text dubious, see Hup Che Bae); moral qualities ascribed to: — as arrogant 12:5 (compare 12:4 above); as devising injuries, ל תַּחְשֹׁב ׳הַוּוֺת 52:4 , compare ׳לְ הַוֺת Prov 17:4 ; ׳ל מִרְמָה תַּצְמִיד Psa 50:19 nectere fraudem ; ל נְצֹר ׳מֵרָ֑ע 34:14 ׅ || מִרְמָה מִדַּבֵּר (וּשְׂפָתֶיךָ ; often of lying tongue: שֶׁקֶר לְשׁוֺן Prov 6:17 ; 12:19 ; 21:6 ; 26:28 ; Psa 109:2 ; ׳לְ מִרְמָה 52:6 ; ׳לָ רְמִיָּה Micah 6:12 ; Psa 120:2 ; 120:3 ; ׳לְ תַּרְמִית Zeph 3:13 ; ׳לְ תַּהְמֻּכוֺת Prov 10:31 , and בִּל ׳נֶהְמָּךְ 17:20 ; עֲרוּמִים׳ל Job 15:5 ; also ׳ל דִּבֵּ֑ר מִרְמָה Jer 9:7 ; on the other hand ׳לְ צַדִּיק Prov 10:20 ; ׳ל חֲכָמִים 12:18 ; 15:2 ; לָ ׳מַרְמֵּה 15:4 ; ׳לְ לִמּוּדִים Isa 50:4 . &#8212; Note phrases ל ׳שׁוֺט Job 5:21 scourge of (the) tongue , לְשֹׁנוֺת רִיב Psa 31:21 ; לְשׁוֺנָם מַּלַּג 55:10 : also הַלּ ׳בַּעַל Eccl 10:11 (of serpent-charmer), and ל עַלשְֿׂפַת ׳וַתֵּעֲלוּ Ezek 36:3 . &#8212; On tongue of ׳י (once), see 4 below c. organ of singing, subject of רָנַן Psa 51:16 ; 126:2 ; Isa 35:6 , עָנָה Psa 119:172 . 2 = language Deut 28:49 ; Jer 5:15 and later, namely: Ezek 3:5-6 , ( ל ׳כִּבְדֵי , || שָׂפָה עִמְקֵי , but strike out ᵐ5 Manuscripts Co Sgfr KauAT ), Isa 28:11 (|| שָׂפָה לַעֲגֵי ׳ל, אַחֶרֶת , figurative of ׳י s unintelligible dealings); ל נִלְעַג ֗֗֗ ׳עַם 33:19 (|| שָׂפָה עִמְקֵי ); 66:18 (|| גּוֺיִם ), Zech 8:23 ; Gen 10:5 , 20 , 31 (all P), Neh 13:24 ; Est 1:22 (twice in verse); 3:12 ; 8:9 (twice in verse); Dan 1:4 . 3 tongue of animals: dog Exod 11:7 (J; object of I. חָרַץ q. v.; compare 1b ), Psa 68:24 ; adder Job 20:16 (subjectof תַּהֲרֹג ); crocodile Job 40:25. 4 tongue of fire, devouring, אֵשׁ לְשׁוֺן קַשׁ כֶּאֱכֹל Isa 5:24 ; compare of אֹכָ֑לֶת כְּאֵשׁ וּלְשׁוֺנוֺ ׳י, 30:27 (|| זַעַם מָֽלְאוּ שְׂפָתָיו ). 5 = ( tongue- shaped) wedge of gold Josh 7:21 , 24 (JE). **So Assyrian lišânu ; see Meissn ZAW xxlii {1905}, 151 f. Johns Assyrian Deeds 2, 281 . 6 = ( tongue- shaped) bay of sea Isa 11:15 ; Josh 15:2 , 5 ; 18:19 (all P). לִשָּׁן noun masculine Dan 3:7 tongue ( ᵑ7 Syriac; see Biblical Hebrew לָשׁוֺן , √ לשׁן ); — tongue = language , figurative for people: absolute וְל אֻמָּה ׳עַם 3:29 ; plural emphatic ׳ע ׳א וְלִשָּׁנַיָּא 3:4 ; 3:7 ; 4:31 ; 5:19 ; 6:26 ; 7:14 (compare Biblical Hebrew לָשׁוֺן 2 , Isa 66:18 ). מָא see מָה . below","rootNote":"or לָשֹׁן ; also (in plural) feminine לְשֹׁנָה ; from 3960 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Sam 23 2","keyReferences":["2Sam 23 2","Dan 1 4","Deut 28 49","Eccl 10 11","Esth 1 22","Esth 1 22","Esth 3 12","Esth 8 9"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":117,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Sam 23 2","book":"2Sam","chapter":23,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְשׁוֹנִֽ/י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbsc/Sp1cs"},{"reference":"Dan 1 4","book":"Dan","chapter":1,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וּ/לְשׁ֥וֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncbsc"},{"reference":"Deut 28 49","book":"Deut","chapter":28,"verse":49,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְשֹׁנֽ/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcbsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"Eccl 10 11","book":"Eccl","chapter":10,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"הַ/לָּשֽׁוֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTd/Ncbsa"},{"reference":"Esth 1 22","book":"Esth","chapter":1,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כִּ/לְשׁוֹנ֑/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncbsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"Esth 1 22","book":"Esth","chapter":1,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כִּ/לְשׁ֥וֹן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncbsc"},{"reference":"Esth 3 12","book":"Esth","chapter":3,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כִּ/לְשׁוֹנ֑/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncbsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"Esth 8 9","book":"Esth","chapter":8,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"כִּ/לְשֹׁנ֑/וֹ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Ncbsc/Sp3ms"},{"reference":"Esth 8 9","book":"Esth","chapter":8,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/כִ/לְשׁוֹנָֽ/ם","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/R/Ncbsc/Sp3mp"},{"reference":"Exod 4 10","book":"Exod","ch